RefineKV

This standalone package extracts the stable ConditionBlock/diag-ell algorithm
and split attention implementation from the interattn research repository.
The original repository's MIT license notice is retained in LICENSE.

Implementation origins, relative to the original repository:

- llama/script/analysis/condition_block_ball/stable_diag_ell.py
  Centered radius construction, stable condition terms, selection kernels,
  and fused representative selection.
- llama/script/analysis/condition_block_ball/triton_finalize_v3.py
  Selected-page/suffix attention and online-softmax reduction.
- llama/script/analysis/condition_block_gen/methods/condition_block_triton_impl/core.py
  Selection-statistic reduction and continuous page layout.
- llama/script/analysis/condition_block_ball/prompt_anchor_union/runtime.py
  Memory-efficient page construction and prompt-anchor union semantics.

Inactive experiment branches were removed from the extracted kernels.
Request state, explicit configuration, the tensor API, the PyTorch reference,
and the registered Transformers integration are packaged independently.
No runtime import of the original repository is required.

PyTorch, Transformers, and Triton are external dependencies distributed
under their respective licenses.
